## Error Handling Patterns

### Service Layer Error Handling

```php
// ✅ Always return ServiceResponse, never throw exceptions to controllers
if (!file_exists($file_path)) {
    return ServiceResponse::failure(
        __('File not found.', 'debug-suite'),
        'file_not_found',
        ['path' => $file_path] // Context data for debugging
    );
}

// ✅ Success responses with structured data
return ServiceResponse::success([
    'entries' => $log_entries,
    'total' => count($log_entries),
    'file_path' => $log_file,
    'stats' => $file_stats
]);
```

### Frontend Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ Handle API errors gracefully with toast notifications
import { useToast } from '@/components/base/toast';

try {
    const response = await apiFetch<ApiResponse>({
        path: addQueryArgs('/debug-suite/v1/logs', { limit: 100 })
    });

    if (response.success) {
        setData(response.data);
        toast.success(__('Data loaded successfully', 'debug-suite'));
    } else {
        setError(response.message);
        toast.error(response.message);
    }
} catch (error) {
    const message = __('An unexpected error occurred', 'debug-suite');
    setError(message);
    toast.error(message);
}
```

## Testing Standards

### PHP Unit Tests

```php
/**
 * @covers \DebugSuite\Services\FileLogsService
 * @group services
 * @group unit
 */
class FileLogsServiceTest extends TestCase {

    public function test_get_log_entries_success(): void {
        $service = new FileLogsService();
        $result = $service->get_log_entries(['limit' => 10]);

        $this->assert_service_result_success($result);
        $this->assertArrayHasKey('entries', $result->get_data());
    }

    public function test_service_failure_with_context(): void {
        $result = ServiceResponse::failure('Test error', 'test_code', ['key' => 'value']);

        $this->assert_service_result_failure($result);
        $this->assert_service_result_error_code($result, 'test_code');
    }
}
```

### Integration Tests

```php
/**
 * @covers \DebugSuite\API\FileLogsController
 * @group api
 * @group integration
 */
class FileLogsControllerTest extends DebugSuiteTestCase {

    public function test_get_logs_endpoint(): void {
        $this->create_admin_user();

        $request = new WP_REST_Request('GET', '/debug-suite/v1/logs');
        $response = rest_get_server()->dispatch($request);

        $this->assertEquals(200, $response->get_status());
    }
}
```

## Performance & Security

### Security Practices

```php
// ✅ Always sanitize and validate input
$safe_path = $this->sanitize_path($relative_path);
if (!$this->is_path_safe($full_path)) {
    return ServiceResponse::failure('Invalid path', 'invalid_path');
}

// ✅ Check permissions in controllers
if (!current_user_can('manage_options')) {
    return new WP_Error('permission_denied', 'Insufficient permissions');
}
```

### Performance Optimization

```php
// ✅ Use container singleton pattern for expensive operations
$container->add([
    ExpensiveService::class => $container->object(ExpensiveService::class)
]);

// ✅ Implement caching for file operations
private array $file_cache = [];
```

